{% comment %}
  Server-rendered from Shopify's own `cart` object, so the count is correct
  on first paint — before theme.js has run at all — rather than starting at
  zero and waiting on a client-side fetch the way the headless GitHub Pages
  version had to (it had no server-rendered cart to read).
{% endcomment %}
<button type="button" class="cart-toggle" data-cart-toggle aria-label="Order" aria-haspopup="dialog">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="M5 8h14l-1.2 10.2a2 2 0 0 1-2 1.8H8.2a2 2 0 0 1-2-1.8L5 8Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    <path d="M8.5 8V6a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 7 0v2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
  </svg>
  <span class="cart-toggle__count" data-cart-count{% if cart.item_count == 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
</button>
{%- comment -%}
  Adding to cart is a commit. Sighted users get the badge and the drawer
  opening; without this a screen reader got nothing at all. Kept outside the
  button so the announcement is not read as part of its label, and phrased as
  a sentence rather than a bare digit.
{%- endcomment -%}
<span class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-cart-announce>
  {%- if cart.item_count == 1 -%}1 item in your order
  {%- elsif cart.item_count > 1 -%}{{ cart.item_count }} items in your order
  {%- endif -%}
</span>
